1043 #edb/ref 17592186148263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147676 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147676 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147676 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147676 #edb/ref 1045 "Evaluating Exponents With Fractional Bases" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147676 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186148262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147676 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147676 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "6c51ae60-8fe3-549c-b67d-8a5d1d77e244" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148262 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148262 #edb/ref 1061 176246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148262 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "60be27f5-6cd2-5965-9278-49fd234a2f60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148262 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186148793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148263 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148263 #edb/ref 1061 176247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148263 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e85e09d4-1db1-5d14-8624-322891620292" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148263 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148264 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148264 #edb/ref 1061 176251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148264 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "019a4899-8126-5053-9f04-d4a2cdb37169" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148264 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148265 #edb/ref 1061 176255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148265 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "69440fb9-e705-54f8-8912-a6132bdc4df6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148265 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148793 #edb/ref 1064 "We can use our knowledge of fraction multiplication to square fractions.\n\nFor example, let's evaluate the following squared fraction:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2\n$$\n\nFirst, we write\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2\n$$\n\nwith multiplication signs:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{3}{5})^{2} = \\frac{3}{5} \\cdot \\frac{3}{5}_(⏟)_([math]\\color{blue}2[/math] times)\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the product of the two fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(\\frac{3}{5})^{2} &= \\frac{3}{5} \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3 \\cdot 3}{5 \\cdot 5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{25}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2= \\dfrac{9}{25}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148793 #edb/ref 1065 8806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148793 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f0e87aeb-338c-5f8d-be18-59b85ed28aac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148793 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505098 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186505892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505098 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505098 #edb/ref 1045 "Decimal and Fraction Operations Applied to Commercial Settings" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505098 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186505892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505098 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "66ea1ffa-aceb-57da-af76-bf51c4bf7282" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505123 #edb/ref 1080 "0.46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505123 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505123 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "09de715f-588e-5d61-86ff-27d04fa29d98" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505276 #edb/ref 1080 "62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505276 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505276 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "55912364-c928-5e09-9952-20f2493aa37e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505290 #edb/ref 1080 "0.24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505290 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505290 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5c281